# Copy to .env.deploy and fill in (never commit .env.deploy).
#
# FTP_HOST: hostname only, e.g. ftp.example.com
# FTP_REMOTE_DIR: folder ON THE SERVER where this app’s files go (see below).
# Optional: FTP_PORT (default 21), FTP_USE_TLS (1 = try explicit TLS if host supports it)
#
# ── Subdirectory on your site ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# To serve the app at https://yoursite.com/architrek/ (not at the domain root):
# 1. In your hosting panel, create a folder under the web root, e.g. "architrek".
# 2. Set FTP_REMOTE_DIR to that folder’s full path on the server. Names vary by host:
#    /public_html/architrek
#    /www/architrek
#    /htdocs/architrek
#    /domains/yoursite.com/public_html/architrek
# 3. Deploy: ./scripts/deploy-ftp.sh uploads index.html, ui/, data/, … into that folder.
# 4. Open https://yoursite.com/architrek/ (trailing slash is best for relative URLs).
#
# If you instead set FTP_REMOTE_DIR to the site root (e.g. /public_html), the app
# loads at https://yoursite.com/ — only do that if no other site lives there.
#
# ── HTTPS (padlock in the browser) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Turn on a free certificate (Let’s Encrypt or similar) in the hosting control panel
# for your domain, and enable “force HTTPS” if the panel offers it. The repo includes
# .htaccess with an HTTP→HTTPS redirect for Apache; nginx-only hosts use the panel.

FTP_HOST=
FTP_USER=
FTP_PASS=
FTP_REMOTE_DIR=

# FTP_PORT=21
# FTP_USE_TLS=0
